{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e5c1bee958e39c21","name":"Projectile Appendage","source":{"id":"source:reference-e5c1bee958e39c21","title":"Projectile Appendage","revision":21086,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:08:14Z","sha256":"356354747da25f89af4db4eb42d60de26168a7940d4a335462e8bb3bfb4a6977","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21086","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Projectile%20Appendage&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e5c1bee958e39c21","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," Appendage Cost x 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," (2 x ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cost Factor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cost_Factor"},") Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Licensed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Licensed"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droids","referenceId":"reference:e0ba1be2d9a6a37a"}," are programmed for combat and security, but other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," can defend themselves as well. A popular modification is a Projectile Appendage, usually a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hand"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hand","referenceId":"reference:fa18c06733fbbf41"}," on humanoid ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},". When the projectile is activated, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Appendage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Appendage"}," flies toward the target. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," might use a Projectile Appendage in order to stun an aggressor or knock a blaster away rather than risking destruction in a blaster fight. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The basic package is a tension-spring device that costs 250 credits to install. A Projectile Appendage is considered to be a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapon (Ranged)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapon_(Ranged)"}," that deals 2d8 damage. Additionally, the Projectile Appendage can be used to make a ranged ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disarm"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disarm","referenceId":"reference:0449aa195af99b14"}," attempt against a target within 6 squares. \n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
